<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yervandashat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yervandashat was an ancient Armenian city at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a> and Akhurian rivers, founded by the Orontid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-iv">Orontes IV</a> around the end of the 3rd century BCE as his new capital in place of Armavir. It remained a royal city until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxias-i">Artaxias I</a> moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxata">Artaxata</a>. Its ruins lie on the modern border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>.</p></div>
